Roland, I have reviewed the 2011 file on this and Ardsley's position is att=
ached on letterhead. Summarizing it here for the record.<br />
<br />
The moisture mitigation system specified in Section 09 05 61 was deleted at=
 Ardsley's written direction of May 17, 2011, over VAA's written recommenda=
tion of April 6, 2011, and in reliance on our own consultant's assessment. =
That direction expressly accepted responsibility for future flooring perfor=
mance issues arising from slab moisture. The pantry failure is exactly that=
.<br />
<br />
Ardsley is funding the remediation of the pantry and wellness room in the a=
mount of $88,400 and is making no claim against VAA in connection with it. =
Our contractor starts October 21.<br />
<br />
I would rather write this letter once than twice, so I will also say the ob=
vious. If the pantry is doing this at year two, the rest of Levels 12 throu=
gh 19 will do it eventually. That is our exposure, not yours, and it is on =
the record as ours.
